{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>When Pharaoh speaks to you, saying.</b> HaShem, blessed be He, informed Moses that Pharaoh was destined to ask of him a sign, and a man is not established as a prophet until he gives a sign or wonder, or until a prophet who is already confirmed in his prophecy testifies concerning him." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> כי ידבר אליכם פרעה — 'Give yourselves a sign.' The righteous ask for a sign — all the more so the wicked! For thus we find in the case of Noah: after the Holy One, blessed be He, saved him from the Flood, He said to him (Genesis 9:15): ״ולא יהיה עוד המים למבול לשחת כל בשר.״ Noah said to Him: Give me a sign. He said to him: ״את קשתי נתתי בענן והיתה לאות ברית״ and so forth. And likewise Hezekiah, when he fell ill — the Holy One, blessed be He, sent Isaiah to him; he said (Isaiah 38:8): מה אות כי אעלה בית ה' — 'What is the sign that I shall go up to the House of HaShem?' He said to him: 'Behold, I shall make the shadow of the sundial turn back.' Hence one may say: כי ידבר אליכם פרעה."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:42.982429089Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}